D('afflicting',{etymology:{origin:'afflicting 是 afflict 的现在分词形容词；afflict 经古法语来自拉丁语 affligere“击倒、使痛苦”，由 ad- 与 fligere“打击”构成。',prefix:'ad-',root:'flig-',suffix:'-ing',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/afflicting'},contexts:[{domain:'疾病 · 痛苦影响',senseId:'afflicting.s1',en:'The afflicting illness forced the village clinic to move patients into a temporary ward, where nurses could monitor breathing throughout the night.',zh:'这种令人痛苦的疾病迫使乡村诊所把患者转入临时病房，护士在那里整夜监测他们的呼吸。',structure:'The afflicting illness forced the village clinic to move patients into a temporary ward / where nurses could monitor breathing throughout the night.',grammar:'afflicting 修饰 illness，表示给人带来痛苦、疾病或严重麻烦。',rationale:'疾病使患者承受痛苦并需要持续照护，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','The disease was afflicting on residents throughout the winter.','The disease was afflicting residents throughout the winter.','afflict 是及物动词，直接接受影响的人，不在宾语前加 on。')],quiz:[q('afflicting',1,1,'An afflicting illness is one that?','causes suffering or serious trouble','improves a patient’s health immediately','allows free entry to a clinic','afflicting.s1 指带来痛苦或严重麻烦的。'),q('afflicting',2,1,'A drought is described as afflicting several farms. It is?','causing hardship for the farms','helping the farms produce more water','a person who advises the farmers','afflict somebody 表示使其遭受痛苦或困境。'),q('afflicting',3,1,'Choose the correct verb pattern.','a disease afflicting many people','a disease afflicting on many people','a disease afflicting to many people','afflict 直接接宾语，通常不接 on/to。'),q('afflicting',4,1,'Which situation is most likely to be called afflicting?','a painful disease disrupting daily life','a pleasant surprise at a party','a well-designed aircraft wing','该形容词适用于造成痛苦或困难的事物。')]});
D('affliction',{etymology:{origin:'affliction 由 afflict 加名词后缀 -ion 构成，指痛苦、苦难或折磨；afflict 来自拉丁语 affligere“击倒、使痛苦”。',prefix:null,root:'flig-',suffix:'-ion',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/affliction'},contexts:[{domain:'健康 · 长期痛苦',senseId:'affliction.s1',en:'For years, recurring migraines were her greatest affliction, disrupting work whenever bright light and noise triggered another severe attack.',zh:'多年来，反复发作的偏头痛是她最大的痛苦，每当强光和噪声引发新一轮严重发作，工作就会受到影响。',structure:'For years / recurring migraines were her greatest affliction / disrupting work whenever bright light and noise triggered another attack.',grammar:'affliction 是可数或抽象名词，指痛苦、困扰或疾病造成的折磨。',rationale:'反复偏头痛让她长期承受痛苦，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The family’s main affliction were the recurring migraines.','The family’s main affliction was the recurring migraines.','中心主语 affliction 为单数，谓语用 was。')],quiz:[q('affliction',1,1,'A serious affliction is?','a state of pain or distress','a permission to enter a building','a study of airflow','affliction.s1 指痛苦、折磨或苦难。'),q('affliction',2,1,'A chronic illness became his greatest affliction. The illness caused?','ongoing distress or misery','a pleasant holiday','an immediate promotion','affliction 描述使人长期受苦的状态。'),q('affliction',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a painful affliction','an afflictionly pain','to afflictation a person','affliction 是表示痛苦状态的名词。'),q('affliction',4,1,'A person speaks of an affliction that disrupts daily life. The person means?','a source of serious suffering','a source of free admittance','a kind of aerodynamic study','affliction 的核心是痛苦和困扰。')]});
D('afield',{etymology:{origin:'afield 由旧式副词前缀 a- 与 field 构成，早期可指在田野上；后来也表示离开常处或题目很远。',prefix:'a-',root:'field',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/afield'},contexts:[{domain:'探索 · 远行',senseId:'afield.s1',en:'The botanist traveled far afield to compare alpine plants with the specimens growing in the coastal reserve near her laboratory.',zh:'植物学家远赴他乡，把高山植物与实验室附近海岸保护区中的标本进行比较。',structure:'The botanist traveled far afield / to compare alpine plants with specimens / growing in the coastal reserve near her laboratory.',grammar:'far afield 表示到远离平常地点的地方，也可比喻偏离话题。',rationale:'植物学家前往远方进行比较，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'田野 · 户外',senseId:'afield.s2',en:'At dawn, the shepherd was already afield with the flock, checking the fences before the animals reached the narrow road.',zh:'黎明时，牧羊人已经带着羊群在田野上，赶在牲畜到达狭窄公路前检查围栏。',structure:'At dawn / the shepherd was already afield with the flock / checking the fences before the animals reached the road.',grammar:'afield 也可作副词，表示在田野或户外区域。',rationale:'人物在田野中放牧并检查围栏，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','The search team traveled to afield to inspect the distant ridge.','The search team traveled far afield to inspect the distant ridge.','常见搭配是 far afield；afield 前不加表示方向的 to。')],quiz:[q('afield',1,1,'A researcher travels far afield. The researcher goes?','a long way from the usual place','only to the next room','back to the same desk','afield.s1 指远离常处的地方。'),q('afield',2,2,'A shepherd is out afield with the flock. The shepherd is?','in the fields or open country','inside a locked office','on an aircraft wing','afield.s2 可表示在田野或户外。'),q('afield',3,1,'Complete the common phrase: “They searched far ___.”','afield','to afield','afieldly','far afield 是表示远行的常见搭配。'),q('afield',4,1,'If a discussion wanders afield, it?','moves away from the main topic','becomes more aerodynamic','is formally admitted','afield 可比喻偏离当前话题。')]});
D('afoul',{etymology:{origin:'afoul 由 a- 与 foul 构成，原有船只相撞、缠绕的航海用法；现代常见于 run afoul of，表示与规则或人发生冲突。',prefix:'a-',root:'foul',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/afoul'},contexts:[{domain:'法规 · 冲突',senseId:'afoul.s1',en:'The company ran afoul of the privacy rules after it shared customer records without consent, and regulators ordered an immediate review of its data practices.',zh:'公司未经同意分享客户记录后触犯了隐私规定，监管机构随即要求其立即审查数据做法。',structure:'The company ran afoul of the privacy rules / after it shared customer records without consent / and regulators ordered a review.',grammar:'run afoul of + 规则或人表示违反、触犯或与之发生冲突。',rationale:'未经许可分享记录违反规定，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','The contractor ran afoul with the building code during the renovation.','The contractor ran afoul of the building code during the renovation.','固定搭配是 run afoul of，而不是 run afoul with。')],quiz:[q('afoul',1,1,'A firm runs afoul of a law when it?','violates or conflicts with it','receives permission to enter','adopts it without changes','afoul.s1 指与规则或人发生冲突。'),q('afoul',2,1,'The ship’s ropes became afoul of one another. They became?','tangled together','neatly arranged','aerodynamically shaped','afoul 有缠绕、纠结的用法。'),q('afoul',3,1,'Which phrase is standard?','run afoul of the rules','run afoul at the rules','run afoul with to the rules','常见结构为 run afoul of。'),q('afoul',4,1,'A team that runs afoul of safety regulations has?','come into conflict with them','passed every inspection automatically','adjourned them until Monday','该短语表示触犯规定或与规定冲突。')]});
D('Africa',{etymology:{origin:'Africa 作为地名来自拉丁语 Africa（罗马的 Africa provincia）；该名称更早可能与 Afri 等地名或族名有关，但词源有争议，不能当作定论。',prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/Africa'},contexts:[{domain:'地理 · 大洲',senseId:'Africa.s1',en:'Africa stretches from the Mediterranean coast to the Cape region, and its varied climates support deserts, rain forests, grasslands, and high mountains.',zh:'非洲从地中海沿岸延伸至好望角地区，多样的气候孕育了沙漠、雨林、草原和高山。',structure:'Africa stretches from the Mediterranean coast to the Cape region / and its varied climates support deserts, rain forests, grasslands, and mountains.',grammar:'Africa 是专有名词，指欧洲以南的大洲；专名首字母大写。',rationale:'句子描述整块非洲大陆的地理范围，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'文化 · 历史群体',senseId:'Africa.s2',en:'The exhibition examined Africa’s many literary traditions without treating the continent as culturally uniform, and it featured authors from several regions.',zh:'展览探讨了非洲多样的文学传统，没有把整个大陆视为文化单一的整体，并展出了多个地区的作家。',structure:'The exhibition examined Africa’s many literary traditions / without treating the continent as culturally uniform / and featured authors from several regions.',grammar:'Africa 在文化或历史语境中可概括指非洲国家与人民，但需避免抹平内部差异。',rationale:'讨论涉及非洲各地区的文化群体，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('spelling','The expedition crossed africa from north to south.','The expedition crossed Africa from north to south.','大洲专名 Africa 首字母必须大写。')],quiz:[q('Africa',1,1,'Africa is the continent located largely?','south of Europe','north of the Arctic Circle','inside South America','Africa.s1 指非洲大陆。'),q('Africa',2,2,'A book compares literary traditions across Africa. “Africa” refers to?','African countries and peoples as a broad cultural region','only one city','an aircraft’s flight path','Africa.s2 可在文化或历史语境中概括相关国家与人民。'),q('Africa',3,1,'Choose the standard spelling of the continent’s name.','Africa','africa','Afrikae','专有地名 Africa 首字母大写。'),q('Africa',4,2,'A writer discusses music from several African countries as part of Africa’s heritage. The word Africa refers to?','the continent and its diverse peoples','a single national language only','a naval rank','此语境中 Africa 概括大陆上的多元文化。')]});
D('African',{etymology:{origin:'African 由 Africa 加形容词或人物名词后缀 -an 构成，可指来自非洲的人，也可表示与非洲及其人民有关。',prefix:null,root:'Afric-',suffix:'-an',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/African'},contexts:[{domain:'人物 · 出身',senseId:'African.s1',en:'An African joined the research team after completing fieldwork in her home region, bringing knowledge of local plant names and seasonal harvesting practices.',zh:'一位非洲人完成家乡地区的田野调查后加入研究团队，带来了当地植物名称和季节性采集做法的知识。',structure:'An African joined the research team / after completing fieldwork in her home region / bringing knowledge of local plant names and seasonal practices.',grammar:'African 作可数名词时可指来自非洲的人；an African 首字母大写。',rationale:'人物来自非洲，符合 African.s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'文化 · 相关属性',senseId:'African.s2',en:'The museum’s African art collection includes works from many countries and periods, so the curator labels each object with its specific origin.',zh:'博物馆的非洲艺术藏品涵盖多个国家和时代，因此策展人为每件作品标注了具体来源。',structure:'The museum’s African art collection includes works from many countries and periods / so the curator labels each object with its origin.',grammar:'African 作形容词时表示与非洲或其人民有关。',rationale:'藏品与非洲地区及其艺术传统相关，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('spelling','The museum displayed african textiles from several regions.','The museum displayed African textiles from several regions.','国籍或地区形容词 African 作专名衍生词时首字母大写。')],quiz:[q('African',1,1,'An African is?','a person who comes from Africa','a device used in aeration','someone who adjourns a hearing','African.s1 指来自非洲的人。'),q('African',2,2,'African literature means literature?','related to Africa or its peoples','written only in Europe','made from adobe bricks','African.s2 作形容词表示与非洲有关。'),q('African',3,1,'Which spelling is standard for the nationality adjective?','African','african','africAn','African 是专名衍生词，首字母大写。'),q('African',4,2,'An African historian studies?','history connected with African regions or peoples','only aircraft design','a person’s right of admittance','African 可作形容词指与非洲相关。')]});
D('aftereffect',{etymology:{origin:'aftereffect 是 after + effect 构成的复合名词，指事件或经历之后出现的影响；effect 经法语来自拉丁语 effectus“结果、成效”。',prefix:'after-',root:'fect-',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aftereffect'},contexts:[{domain:'医疗 · 后续影响',senseId:'aftereffect.s1',en:'Fatigue was an aftereffect of the infection that lasted for weeks after the fever ended, so the doctor recommended a gradual return to exercise.',zh:'发烧退去后，疲劳仍持续了数周，是这次感染留下的后效，因此医生建议逐步恢复锻炼。',structure:'Fatigue was an aftereffect of the infection / that lasted for weeks after the fever ended / so the doctor recommended a gradual return to exercise.',grammar:'aftereffect 是可数名词，指稍后出现、往往不受欢迎的影响。',rationale:'疲劳在感染和发烧之后持续出现，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aftereffects of the infection was still noticeable weeks later.','The aftereffects of the infection were still noticeable weeks later.','主语中心词 aftereffects 为复数，谓语应为 were。')],quiz:[q('aftereffect',1,1,'An aftereffect appears?','after an earlier event or experience','before the event begins','only while a person is asleep','aftereffect.s1 指之后产生的影响。'),q('aftereffect',2,1,'Weeks of fatigue after an illness may be?','an aftereffect','an admittance','an aerodynamic feature','后遗疲劳是疾病之后出现的影响。'),q('aftereffect',3,1,'Choose the correct spelling and form.','an aftereffect of treatment','an after affect of treatment','an afterward effecting','aftereffect 是 after + effect 的复合名词。'),q('aftereffect',4,1,'A report studies the aftereffects of a storm. It studies?','later consequences of the storm','the weather before the storm','the storm’s name only','该词指事件之后出现的后续影响。')]});
D('afterlife',{etymology:{origin:'afterlife 由 after + life 构成，字面为今生之后的存在；该词用于宗教或大众信仰中死后的生活。',prefix:'after-',root:'life',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/afterlife'},contexts:[{domain:'宗教 · 死后存在',senseId:'afterlife.s1',en:'The novel imagines an afterlife in which people revisit the choices that shaped their lives, although its characters disagree about whether the place is real.',zh:'小说构想了一种来世，人们会重新面对塑造其一生的选择，尽管书中人物并不确定那个地方是否真实存在。',structure:'The novel imagines an afterlife / in which people revisit the choices that shaped their lives / although its characters disagree about whether it is real.',grammar:'afterlife 是可数名词，指宗教或大众信仰中的死后存在。',rationale:'小说描写死亡之后继续存在的世界，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','Many traditions describe an afterlife in which the dead continues to exist.','Many traditions describe an afterlife in which the dead continue to exist.','the dead 在此指一群人，作复数集合意义，谓语应为 continue。')],quiz:[q('afterlife',1,1,'Belief in an afterlife concerns?','existence after death','the effect of a medicine before it is given','a flight above the clouds','afterlife.s1 指死后的生活或存在。'),q('afterlife',2,1,'A story set in the afterlife takes place?','after the characters have died','before they are born','inside a water-treatment tank','afterlife 的核心时间是死亡之后。'),q('afterlife',3,1,'Which phrase is standard?','belief in an afterlife','belief in an after life-formly','belief on the afterliving','afterlife 是表示死后存在的复合名词。'),q('afterlife',4,1,'A religious text describes the afterlife. It describes?','what may exist after death','how a plane reduces drag','a person’s access to a museum','afterlife 涉及死后的生活或存在。')]});
D('afterwards',{etymology:{origin:'afterwards 由 after 加副词后缀 -ward 与历史性副词 -s 构成，表示在已经提到的时间或事件之后；英美拼写常见 afterwards/afterward。',prefix:'after-',root:'ward',suffix:'-s',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/afterwards'},contexts:[{domain:'时间 · 先后顺序',senseId:'afterwards.s1',en:'They inspected the damaged bridge in the morning and met with residents afterwards, once the engineers had explained which lanes were safe.',zh:'他们上午检查受损桥梁，之后在工程师说明哪些车道安全后与居民会面。',structure:'They inspected the damaged bridge in the morning / and met with residents afterwards / once the engineers had explained which lanes were safe.',grammar:'afterwards 是副词，表示在已提及的事件或时间之后；不能直接带宾语。',rationale:'会面发生在上午检查之后，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','They met afterwards the inspection to discuss the bridge repairs.','They met afterwards, after the inspection, to discuss the bridge repairs.','afterwards 是副词，不能直接接名词宾语 the inspection；可用逗号后另加 after 短语。')],quiz:[q('afterwards',1,1,'If a team eats lunch afterwards, it eats?','after the event already mentioned','before the event begins','instead of eating at all','afterwards.s1 表示在稍后、之后。'),q('afterwards',2,1,'“We will review the report and speak afterwards” means?','the speaking will happen later','the speaking happened first','the report is made of adobe','afterwards 指后续时间。'),q('afterwards',3,1,'Which sentence is correct?','We went home afterwards.','We went home afterwards the meeting.','We afterwards to the meeting went.','afterwards 作副词，不直接接宾语。'),q('afterwards',4,1,'Choose the standard variant pair.','afterwards / afterward','afterwardly / afterwarness','afterwarded / aftering','英式常见 afterwards，美式也常用 afterward。')]});
D('ageism',{etymology:{origin:'ageism 是 age + -ism 构成的词，仿 racism、sexism 表示基于年龄的偏见或歧视；该词由老年学家 Robert Butler 于1969年提出。',prefix:null,root:'age',suffix:'-ism',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/ageism'},contexts:[{domain:'职场 · 年龄歧视',senseId:'ageism.s1',en:'The audit found ageism in hiring records: equally qualified older applicants were repeatedly screened out before interviews, while younger candidates advanced.',zh:'审计在招聘记录中发现年龄歧视：资历相当的年长申请者反复在面试前被筛掉，而年轻候选人却进入下一轮。',structure:'The audit found ageism in hiring records / equally qualified older applicants were repeatedly screened out / while younger candidates advanced.',grammar:'ageism 是不可数名词，指基于年龄的偏见或歧视。',rationale:'申请者因年龄而受到不平等筛选，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('spelling','The report documented ageisim in the promotion process.','The report documented ageism in the promotion process.','正确拼写是 ageism，age 后直接接 -ism，不插入 i。')],quiz:[q('ageism',1,1,'Ageism is discrimination based on a person’s?','age','flight experience','right to enter a building','ageism.s1 指基于年龄的偏见或歧视。'),q('ageism',2,1,'Rejecting qualified applicants only because they are older may be?','ageism','aeration','admittance','按年龄排斥合格者属于年龄歧视。'),q('ageism',3,1,'Choose the correct spelling.','ageism','ageisim','agismism','ageism 由 age 和 -ism 构成。'),q('ageism',4,1,'A policy is criticized for ageism when it?','treats people unfairly because of age','offers the same access to everyone','changes the timing of a meeting','年龄歧视涉及基于年龄的不公正待遇。')]});
D('agglutinate',{etymology:{origin:'agglutinate 于17世纪初来自拉丁语 agglutinare“粘在一起”，由 ad-“到、一起”与 glutinare“用胶粘”构成，后者关联 gluten“胶”。',prefix:'ad-',root:'glutin-',suffix:'-ate',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/agglutinate'},contexts:[{domain:'生物 · 凝集',senseId:'agglutinate.s1',en:'When the incompatible samples were mixed, the antibodies caused the red blood cells to agglutinate into visible clumps at the bottom of the tube.',zh:'不相容的样本混合后，抗体使红细胞凝集成团，在试管底部形成可见的沉淀。',structure:'When the incompatible samples were mixed / the antibodies caused the red blood cells to agglutinate into visible clumps / at the bottom of the tube.',grammar:'agglutinate 可作及物或不及物动词，表示使颗粒粘结成团。',rationale:'红细胞彼此聚集并粘成团块，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'语言 · 词素粘合',senseId:'agglutinate.s2',en:'In an agglutinate language, a long word may contain several clearly separable morphemes, each adding one grammatical meaning to the stem.',zh:'在黏着语中，一个长词可能含有多个清晰可分的词素，每个词素都给词干增加一种语法意义。',structure:'In an agglutinate language / a long word may contain several clearly separable morphemes / each adding one grammatical meaning to the stem.',grammar:'agglutinate 也可形容由黏合词素形成的语言结构。',rationale:'词素按序粘合、各自表达语法意义，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The antibody agglutinate the cells into clumps during the test.','The antibody agglutinates the cells into clumps during the test.','单数主语 the antibody 作一般现在时主语，谓语需加 -s。')],quiz:[q('agglutinate',1,1,'Particles agglutinate when they?','stick or clump together','separate into individual gases','are admitted to a room','agglutinate.s1 指使部分粘结成团。'),q('agglutinate',2,2,'An agglutinate language builds words by?','joining morphemes that each carry meaning','removing every grammatical ending','using only aircraft terms','agglutinate.s2 描写词素粘合构词的语言类型。'),q('agglutinate',3,1,'Which sentence uses the verb correctly?','The reagent caused the cells to agglutinate.','The reagent agglutinatingly the cells.','The reagent was an agglutination the cells.','cause + object + to agglutinate 是自然动词结构。'),q('agglutinate',4,2,'If a blood sample agglutinates, it forms?','clumps of cells','a smooth aerodynamic surface','a later aftereffect','该动词表示聚集并粘结成团。')]});
D('aggravating',{etymology:{origin:'aggravating 是 aggravate 的现在分词形容词；aggravate 来自拉丁语 aggravare“使更重、加重”，由 ad- 与 gravis“重”构成。',prefix:'ad-',root:'grav-',suffix:'-ing',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aggravating'},contexts:[{domain:'健康 · 症状恶化',senseId:'aggravating.s1',en:'The damp weather was aggravating his joint pain, so the clinician suggested keeping a symptom diary and adjusting the timing of his medication.',zh:'潮湿天气加重了他的关节疼痛，因此临床医生建议记录症状，并调整服药时间。',structure:'The damp weather was aggravating his joint pain / so the clinician suggested keeping a symptom diary / and adjusting medication timing.',grammar:'aggravating 修饰 weather 或 illness 时表示使问题变得更严重。',rationale:'潮湿天气令原有疼痛恶化，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'日常 · 恼人',senseId:'aggravating.s2',en:'The printer’s repeated paper jams were aggravating, especially because the team had to submit the application before the office closed.',zh:'打印机反复卡纸很恼人，尤其团队必须在办公室关门前提交申请。',structure:'The printer’s repeated paper jams were aggravating / especially because the team had to submit the application / before the office closed.',grammar:'aggravating 作表语形容词，也可表示使人恼火、烦躁。',rationale:'反复故障令人烦恼，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-formation','The repeated delay was aggravate for everyone waiting in line.','The repeated delay was aggravating for everyone waiting in line.','was 后需要形容词 aggravating；aggravate 是动词原形。')],quiz:[q('aggravating',1,1,'A factor that aggravates an injury?','makes it more serious','heals it completely','admits it to a building','aggravating.s1 表示使病痛或困难恶化。'),q('aggravating',2,2,'A printer that jams every few minutes is?','extremely annoying','aerodynamic','an afterlife','aggravating.s2 可表示恼人的、令人烦躁的。'),q('aggravating',3,1,'Complete: “The delay was ___ to the passengers.”','aggravating','aggravate','aggravationly','was 后应使用形容词 aggravating。'),q('aggravating',4,2,'Which is an aggravating factor for a rash?','a new detergent that makes it worse','a cream that clears it','an appointment that ended yesterday','aggravating 可表示令已有问题更严重的。')]});
D('aggregated',{etymology:{origin:'aggregated 是 aggregate 的过去分词形容词；aggregate 来自拉丁语 aggregare“聚集成群”，由 ad- 与 grex/gregis“群、羊群”构成。',prefix:'ad-',root:'greg-',suffix:'-ed',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aggregated'},contexts:[{domain:'数据 · 汇总',senseId:'aggregated.s1',en:'The dashboard displayed aggregated sales from all twelve branches, allowing managers to compare the company’s total performance without exposing individual customer records.',zh:'仪表盘显示了十二家分店汇总后的销售数据，使经理能够比较公司总体表现，同时不泄露单个客户记录。',structure:'The dashboard displayed aggregated sales from all twelve branches / allowing managers to compare total performance / without exposing individual records.',grammar:'aggregated 修饰 sales，表示来自多个项目并合并成整体的。',rationale:'各分店数据被汇总为公司整体结果，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aggregated figures from all branches was published yesterday.','The aggregated figures from all branches were published yesterday.','主语 figures 为复数，应使用 were。')],quiz:[q('aggregated',1,1,'Aggregated sales figures are?','combined from separate records','kept as one uncombined receipt','a type of emotional response','aggregated.s1 指将多项数据合并成整体。'),q('aggregated',2,1,'A report gives aggregated responses from every district. It gives?','a combined total or summary','each person’s private answer separately','a future afterlife','aggregate 表示聚合多个独立项目。'),q('aggregated',3,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','aggregated data','aggregate dataing','aggregatedly data','aggregated 可作过去分词形容词修饰 data。'),q('aggregated',4,1,'Why publish aggregated customer statistics?','to show overall patterns without listing each person','to expose each customer’s name','to delay the statistics forever','汇总数据呈现总体情况而不逐条列出个人信息。')]});
D('aggressiveness',{etymology:{origin:'aggressiveness 由 aggressive 加名词后缀 -ness 构成；aggressive 经拉丁语 aggressio/aggredi 来自 ad- + gradi“迈步、走向”，早期有主动进攻义。',prefix:'ad-',root:'grad-',suffix:'-ness',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aggressiveness'},contexts:[{domain:'行为 · 敌意',senseId:'aggressiveness.s1',en:'The review noted the player’s aggressiveness toward opponents, including repeated threats after the referee had already issued a warning.',zh:'评估记录了这名球员对对手的敌意，包括裁判已经警告后仍反复威胁对方。',structure:'The review noted the player’s aggressiveness toward opponents / including repeated threats / after the referee had already issued a warning.',grammar:'aggressiveness 是抽象名词，可指敌对言行或好斗程度。',rationale:'反复威胁对手体现敌意和攻击性，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'工作 · 进取',senseId:'aggressiveness.s2',en:'The startup’s aggressiveness in pursuing new contracts helped it expand quickly, though its managers still checked each bid for financial risk.',zh:'这家初创公司积极争取新合同，帮助业务迅速扩张，不过经理仍会检查每份投标的财务风险。',structure:'The startup’s aggressiveness in pursuing new contracts helped it expand quickly / though managers still checked each bid for financial risk.',grammar:'aggressiveness 也可褒义地表示工作或竞争中的积极进取。',rationale:'企业主动争取机会但仍评估风险，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The team’s aggressiveness were clear in its repeated threats.','The team’s aggressiveness was clear in its repeated threats.','中心名词 aggressiveness 是单数，谓语用 was。')],quiz:[q('aggressiveness',1,1,'Aggressiveness toward rivals may involve?','hostile words or actions','a natural liking for a language','a later effect of medicine','aggressiveness.s1 指敌意或好斗行为。'),q('aggressiveness',2,2,'A company shows positive aggressiveness when it?','energetically pursues work or competition','attacks its customers','refuses every opportunity','aggressiveness.s2 可褒义表示积极进取。'),q('aggressiveness',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','aggressiveness in pursuing new markets','aggressivenessly pursue markets','an aggressive of the market','aggressiveness 是抽象名词，可与 in pursuing 连用。'),q('aggressiveness',4,2,'A report criticizes a player’s aggressiveness after threats. It criticizes?','hostile conduct','careful advice','skillful aerodynamics','该语境下 aggressiveness 指对人的攻击性。')]});
D('aghast',{etymology:{origin:'aghast 于中古英语出现，常被认为与古英语 gast“精神、幽灵”及“使惊恐”一系有关；具体构词演变有不确定性，故不作更细拆分。',prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aghast'},contexts:[{domain:'震惊 · 突发事故',senseId:'aghast.s1',en:'The hikers stood aghast when the bridge railing collapsed beside them, then backed away slowly and called the rescue team from stable ground.',zh:'桥栏在徒步者身旁坍塌时，他们惊呆了，随后慢慢退到安全处并联系救援队。',structure:'The hikers stood aghast / when the bridge railing collapsed beside them / then backed away slowly and called the rescue team.',grammar:'aghast 作表语形容词，表示突然震惊、惊骇；常与 at/by 或从句搭配。',rationale:'突发坍塌使徒步者当场惊骇，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','She was aghast the extent of the damage after the storm.','She was aghast at the extent of the damage after the storm.','aghast 后描述令人震惊的对象时，通常用 at。')],quiz:[q('aghast',1,1,'A person stands aghast after seeing a serious accident. The person is?','suddenly shocked and horrified','calmly pleased','a person who promotes a policy','aghast.s1 指突然震惊、惊骇。'),q('aghast',2,1,'Which situation would leave a witness aghast?','a ceiling collapsing without warning','a familiar cup of tea','a routine note from an advisor','突如其来的危险事故容易使人惊骇。'),q('aghast',3,1,'Choose the standard construction.','aghast at the news','aghast to the news','aghasted of the news','常见结构是 aghast at。'),q('aghast',4,1,'A witness looked aghast when the lights went out and an alarm sounded. The witness looked?','stunned with shock','relaxed and sleepy','ready to buy an advertisement','aghast 表示被突发事件吓住或震惊。')]});
D('agile',{etymology:{origin:'agile 于15世纪中期经法语 agile 来自拉丁语 agilis“灵活、敏捷”，源自 agere“驱动、行动”；该词既可指动作快，也可指思维灵活。',prefix:null,root:'ag-',suffix:'-ile',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/agile'},contexts:[{domain:'运动 · 身体灵活',senseId:'agile.s1',en:'The agile goalkeeper changed direction in one step and blocked the low shot before it slipped inside the post.',zh:'敏捷的守门员一步便变换方向，在低平球滚进门柱前将其挡出。',structure:'The agile goalkeeper changed direction in one step / and blocked the low shot / before it slipped inside the post.',grammar:'agile 修饰 goalkeeper，表示身体移动快且灵活。',rationale:'守门员迅速变向完成扑救，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'思维 · 应变能力',senseId:'agile.s2',en:'An agile analyst reorganized the forecast when new figures arrived, testing several explanations before presenting the revised estimate to the board.',zh:'新数据到来后，思维敏捷的分析师重新整理预测，先检验多种解释，再向董事会提交修订估算。',structure:'An agile analyst reorganized the forecast when new figures arrived / testing several explanations / before presenting the revised estimate.',grammar:'agile 也可形容思维反应快、善于解决问题。',rationale:'分析师快速调整推理并检验解释，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The agile cats moves quickly through the narrow obstacle course.','The agile cats move quickly through the narrow obstacle course.','复数主语 cats 应搭配动词原形 move。')],quiz:[q('agile',1,1,'An agile dancer can?','move quickly and bend easily','remain unable to change direction','measure water aeration','agile.s1 指身体动作敏捷灵活。'),q('agile',2,2,'An agile mind can?','think quickly and solve problems','avoid understanding new facts','fly without an aircraft','agile.s2 指头脑反应快、灵活。'),q('agile',3,1,'Which phrase is correct?','an agile athlete','an agility athlete','an agilely athlete','agile 是形容词，修饰 athlete。'),q('agile',4,2,'A team uses an agile approach when it?','adapts quickly as conditions change','refuses to revise any plan','waits until every opportunity is gone','agile 可比喻灵活应变。')]});
D('agility',{etymology:{origin:'agility 由 agile 加名词后缀 -ity 构成；agile 来自拉丁语 agilis“敏捷的”，与 agere“行动、驱动”有关。',prefix:null,root:'ag-',suffix:'-ity',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/agility'},contexts:[{domain:'运动 · 灵活性',senseId:'agility.s1',en:'The gymnast’s agility let her land from the uneven bars, recover her balance, and move directly into the next tumbling pass.',zh:'体操运动员的灵活性使她从高低杠落地后迅速恢复平衡，并直接接上下一组翻腾动作。',structure:'The gymnast’s agility let her land from the uneven bars / recover her balance / and move into the next tumbling pass.',grammar:'agility 是表示身体或思维敏捷性的不可数名词；let + 宾语 + 动词原形。',rationale:'落地后快速恢复和衔接动作展示身体灵活性，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The athlete’s agility allow her to change direction quickly.','The athlete’s agility allows her to change direction quickly.','单数名词 agility 作主语，谓语需用 allows。')],quiz:[q('agility',1,1,'A gymnast’s agility helps her?','move and change position quickly','stay frozen in one position','administer a policy','agility.s1 指身体动作的敏捷、灵活。'),q('agility',2,1,'Mental agility is the ability to?','think and respond quickly','lift heavy objects only','feel no emotion','agility 也可指思维反应快。'),q('agility',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','agility of movement','agilety of movement','agilityly movement','agility 是表示敏捷性的名词。'),q('agility',4,1,'A player avoids defenders with quick changes of direction. This shows?','agility','adultery','afterlife','迅速变向展示身体灵活性。')]});
D('aging',{etymology:{origin:'aging 是 age 加现在分词后缀 -ing 构成的名词或形容词，表示变老或材料随时间变化；英式拼写常见 ageing，美式常用 aging。',prefix:null,root:'age',suffix:'-ing',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aging'},contexts:[{domain:'材料 · 老化',senseId:'aging.s1',en:'The laboratory accelerated the aging of the rubber seals by exposing them to heat and sunlight, then measured whether they still kept moisture out.',zh:'实验室通过加热和日晒加速橡胶密封圈老化，然后测量它们是否仍能防止水分进入。',structure:'The laboratory accelerated the aging of the rubber seals / by exposing them to heat and sunlight / then measured whether they still kept moisture out.',grammar:'aging 作名词表示变老或材料随时间老化；the aging of + 对象。',rationale:'密封圈经过时间或环境作用发生材料老化，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aging of the rubber seals were measured after the heat test.','The aging of the rubber seals was measured after the heat test.','句子主语中心词 aging 为单数，of the rubber seals 不改变主谓一致。')],quiz:[q('aging',1,1,'Aging is the process of?','becoming older or changing with time','being admitted to a room','joining particles into clumps','aging.s1 指人、动物或材料随时间变老、变化。'),q('aging',2,1,'A laboratory studies the aging of plastic. It studies?','how the material changes over time','how it is advertised','how it becomes an aeroplane','材料老化研究关注长期变化。'),q('aging',3,1,'Which spelling is an accepted British variant?','ageing','agging','ageeing','aging 与 ageing 是常见地区拼写变体。'),q('aging',4,1,'Sunlight can speed the aging of a seal by?','causing it to deteriorate over time','making it younger','granting it admittance','aging 描述随时间发生的变化或衰老。')]});
D('aglow',{etymology:{origin:'aglow 由 a- + glow 构成，表示处于发光、发红或因兴奋而容光焕发的状态；glow 来自古英语 glowan“发热、发光”。',prefix:'a-',root:'glow',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aglow'},contexts:[{domain:'光线 · 发亮',senseId:'aglow.s1',en:'At dusk, the windows were aglow with amber light, making the old stone house visible from the dark road below.',zh:'黄昏时，窗户透出琥珀色的光，使这座老石屋从下方昏暗的道路上也清晰可见。',structure:'At dusk / the windows were aglow with amber light / making the old stone house visible from the dark road below.',grammar:'aglow 常作表语形容词，与 be 动词或 with + 光、颜色等搭配。',rationale:'窗户发出温暖的光，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'情绪 · 喜悦',senseId:'aglow.s1',en:'After the choir finished its first concert, the children were aglow with excitement as their families applauded from the back of the hall.',zh:'合唱团完成首场音乐会后，孩子们因兴奋而容光焕发，家人在大厅后方为他们鼓掌。',structure:'After the choir finished its first concert / the children were aglow with excitement / as their families applauded.',grammar:'aglow with + 情绪可表示因兴奋或喜悦而容光焕发。',rationale:'孩子们的脸因激动而发亮，属于 aglow 的情绪引申义。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','The windows were aglow of warm light after sunset.','The windows were aglow with warm light after sunset.','常见搭配是 aglow with + 光、颜色或情绪，不用 of。')],quiz:[q('aglow',1,1,'A window aglow at night is?','shining or glowing with light','completely unlit','being repaired by an adjuster','aglow.s1 指发出光亮。'),q('aglow',2,1,'A child is aglow with excitement. The child looks?','radiant and visibly happy','angry and motionless','like a stone meteorite','aglow 可比喻因喜悦而容光焕发。'),q('aglow',3,1,'Choose the usual preposition. “aglow ___ candlelight”','with','at by','to for','常用结构为 aglow with。'),q('aglow',4,1,'The mountain peaks were aglow at sunrise. They?','glowed with light or color','were submerged underwater','had been adjourned','aglow 可描述物体发光或呈现鲜亮颜色。')]});
D('agonize',{etymology:{origin:'agonize 于17世纪中期经法语 agoniser 来自希腊语 agonizesthai“在竞赛中奋斗、挣扎”，源自 agōn“竞赛、斗争”；现代常指焦虑苦思或使人极度痛苦。',prefix:null,root:'agon-',suffix:'-ize',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/agonize'},contexts:[{domain:'决策 · 苦苦思索',senseId:'agonize.s1',en:'She agonized over whether to accept the overseas post, weighing the career opportunity against the distance it would put between her and her parents.',zh:'她苦苦思索是否接受海外职位，在职业机会与因此远离父母之间反复权衡。',structure:'She agonized over whether to accept the overseas post / weighing the career opportunity / against the distance from her parents.',grammar:'agonize over + 决策或问题表示长时间焦虑、苦思。',rationale:'人物反复担忧并权衡选择，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'情感 · 造成痛苦',senseId:'agonize.s2',en:'The uncertainty agonized the family for months because officials could not confirm whether the missing boat had reached a safe harbor.',zh:'数月的不确定性令这个家庭极度痛苦，因为官员无法确认失踪的船是否抵达安全港口。',structure:'The uncertainty agonized the family for months / because officials could not confirm / whether the missing boat had reached a safe harbor.',grammar:'agonize 可作及物动词，表示使某人遭受强烈痛苦。',rationale:'持续的不确定使家人承受精神折磨，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','He agonized on the choice for several sleepless nights.','He agonized over the choice for several sleepless nights.','表示为决定而焦虑苦思时，常用 agonize over。')],quiz:[q('agonize',1,1,'She agonized over which job to take. She?','worried about the decision for a long time','made the choice instantly','gave someone permission to enter','agonize.s1 表示长时间焦虑地思考决定。'),q('agonize',2,2,'The delay agonized the waiting family. The delay?','caused them severe distress','made them feel no concern','improved the weather','agonize.s2 表示使某人极度痛苦。'),q('agonize',3,1,'Choose the common preposition: “agonize ___ the decision”','over','to at','by with','表示为决定焦虑苦思时常用 agonize over。'),q('agonize',4,2,'A person agonizing over a choice is?','struggling to decide because of worry','celebrating a decision already made','studying the airflow of a plane','此处 agonize 表示苦苦思索、焦虑不安。')]});
