D('advocator',{etymology:{origin:'advocator 由 advocate 加施事后缀 -or 构成，指为某项主张发声的人；advocate 经法语来自拉丁语 advocatus“被召来帮助的人”，源自动词 advocare。',prefix:null,root:'voc-',suffix:'-or',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/advocator'},contexts:[{domain:'公共事务 · 倡议',senseId:'advocator.s1',en:'An advocator of safer crossings brought collision reports to the council and asked members to add a protected signal before the new school year.',zh:'一名倡导安全过街设施的人把碰撞报告提交给委员会，并要求成员在新学年开始前增设受保护的信号灯。',structure:'An advocator of safer crossings brought collision reports to the council / and asked members to add a protected signal / before the new school year.',grammar:'advocator 是表示拥护或倡议某观点的名词；advocator of + 议题说明其主张。',rationale:'人物为安全过街政策积极发声，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The advocator support a policy requiring safer crossings.','The advocator supports a policy requiring safer crossings.','单数主语 the advocator 在一般现在时需用 supports。')],quiz:[q('advocator',1,1,'An advocator for a policy is someone who?','argues in favor of it','admonishes anyone who mentions it','adjusts the policy’s typeface','advocator.s1 指倡议、拥护某观点的人。'),q('advocator',2,1,'A person speaks at a hearing in support of cleaner rivers. The person is an?','advocator of the cause','admiral of the river','adaptor for the water','为某项政策或事业公开发声的人可称 advocator。'),q('advocator',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','an advocator of reform','an advocator to reforming','an advocateful reform','常见结构是 advocator of + 主张或政策。'),q('advocator',4,1,'The advocator presented evidence for a new rule. The speaker?','supported the proposed rule','opposed every possible rule','was a rule itself','advocator 表示支持并提倡某想法的人。')]});
D('aeration',{etymology:{origin:'aeration 由 aerate 加名词后缀 -ion 构成；aerate 源于 aer“空气”，经拉丁语与希腊语中表示空气的词形传入英语。',prefix:null,root:'aer-',suffix:'-ation',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aeration'},contexts:[{domain:'水处理 · 曝气',senseId:'aeration.s1',en:'The treatment pond uses aeration to add oxygen to the water, helping beneficial bacteria break down waste before the water reaches the wetland.',zh:'处理池通过曝气向水中增加氧气，帮助有益细菌分解废物，再将水排入湿地。',structure:'The treatment pond uses aeration to add oxygen to the water / helping beneficial bacteria break down waste / before the water reaches the wetland.',grammar:'aeration 是不可数名词，表示向水、土壤等引入空气或氧气。',rationale:'池中把空气引入水体，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-formation','The pond was aerated with regular aeratation to increase oxygen.','The pond was aerated with regular aeration to increase oxygen.','名词的正确拼写是 aeration，而不是 aeratation。')],quiz:[q('aeration',1,1,'Aeration in a pond adds what to the water?','air or oxygen','advice about a policy','mud bricks','aeration.s1 指把空气引入水或其他材料。'),q('aeration',2,1,'A gardener loosens soil so air can reach plant roots. This improves?','soil aeration','admittance','adultery','松土让空气进入土壤，是 aeration。'),q('aeration',3,1,'Which sentence uses aeration correctly?','The tank’s aeration keeps oxygen levels stable.','The tank’s aeration is a naval rank.','The tank aerationly stays outdoors.','aeration 是过程名词，可描述供气过程。'),q('aeration',4,1,'Why might wastewater receive aeration?','to introduce oxygen that supports treatment','to remove every molecule of water','to turn it into an aeroplane','曝气把氧气引入水体，常用于处理过程。')]});
D('aero',{etymology:{origin:'aero 是来自希腊语 aer“空气”的组合成分，也可作 informal adjective，表示与飞机或飞行有关；aeroplane 等词保留了这一构词成分。',prefix:null,root:'aer-',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aero'},contexts:[{domain:'航空 · 发动机',senseId:'aero.s1',en:'The museum displayed an aero engine beside the propeller it once powered, with a diagram showing how the design guided air through the cylinders.',zh:'博物馆把航空发动机陈列在它曾驱动的螺旋桨旁，并用图示说明设计如何引导空气流经汽缸。',structure:'The museum displayed an aero engine beside the propeller it once powered / with a diagram showing how the design guided air through the cylinders.',grammar:'aero 在 aero engine 中作与航空有关的前置修饰成分。',rationale:'发动机用于飞机并与飞行相关，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aero engine produce thrust for the test aircraft.','The aero engine produces thrust for the test aircraft.','单数主语 the aero engine 在一般现在时需用 produces。')],quiz:[q('aero',1,1,'In the phrase “aero engine,” aero signals a connection with?','aircraft or flight','advice and counseling','sun-dried building materials','aero.s1 表示与飞机或飞行有关。'),q('aero',2,1,'An aero club is most likely connected with?','aviation','court hearings','food adulteration','aero 常用于航空相关词语中。'),q('aero',3,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','aero engineering','aeroly engineering','an aero of engineering','aero 可作航空领域的组合成分或修饰语。'),q('aero',4,1,'A display about aero design would focus on?','aircraft and flight technology','soil that has no air','marital law','此词形容与航空有关的事物。')]});
D('aerobic',{etymology:{origin:'aerobic 由 aero-“空气、氧气”与 bio- 相关成分及形容词后缀 -ic 构成；该词于19世纪末用于需要氧气的生物过程，后用于健身活动。',prefix:'aero-',root:'bio-',suffix:'-ic',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aerobic'},contexts:[{domain:'生物 · 氧气需求',senseId:'aerobic.s1',en:'These aerobic bacteria thrive in the oxygen-rich layer near the water’s surface, while a different community survives deeper in the oxygen-poor mud.',zh:'这些需氧细菌在水面附近富氧层中繁盛，而另一类微生物则在缺氧的深层泥土中生存。',structure:'These aerobic bacteria thrive in the oxygen-rich layer near the surface / while a different community survives deeper in the oxygen-poor mud.',grammar:'aerobic 修饰 bacteria，表示生长或活动需要氧气；while 对比两种环境。',rationale:'细菌需要氧气才能生长，符合 aerobic.s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'健身 · 有氧运动',senseId:'aerobic.s2',en:'The class alternated brisk steps with low-impact moves, keeping the aerobic pace high enough to raise heart rates without stressing injured knees.',zh:'课程交替安排快步和低冲击动作，使有氧运动强度足以提高心率，同时不增加受伤膝盖的负担。',structure:'The class alternated brisk steps with low-impact moves / keeping the aerobic pace high enough to raise heart rates / without stressing injured knees.',grammar:'aerobic 修饰 exercise、pace 等，描述能持续提高心率的有氧健身活动。',rationale:'动作持续提升心率并作为健身训练，符合 aerobic.s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-choice','The aerobic bacteria grew only in a sealed, oxygen-free chamber.','The anaerobic bacteria grew only in a sealed, oxygen-free chamber.','完全无氧环境适合 anaerobic（厌氧）生物，不符合 aerobic 的需氧义。')],quiz:[q('aerobic',1,1,'Aerobic bacteria need what to live or work?','oxygen','sunlight only','admittance to a building','aerobic.s1 表示需要氧气的生物或过程。'),q('aerobic',2,2,'An aerobic fitness class is designed to?','raise the heart rate through sustained movement','keep participants completely motionless','teach naval ranks','aerobic.s2 指提高心肺活动的有氧健身。'),q('aerobic',3,1,'Which contrast is correct?','aerobic uses oxygen; anaerobic does not require it','aerobic means underwater; anaerobic means airborne','both words mean “without air”','aerobic 强调需要氧气，与 anaerobic 对照。'),q('aerobic',4,2,'A brisk dance workout may be called aerobic because it?','keeps the heart working harder','uses no physical movement','is made of stone','有氧运动会让心脏持续加快工作。')]});
D('aerodynamic',{etymology:{origin:'aerodynamic 由 aero-“空气”与 dynamic“动力的”构成，19世纪形成，指研究空气作用或使空气流过时阻力较小的形状。',prefix:'aero-',root:'dynam-',suffix:'-ic',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aerodynamic'},contexts:[{domain:'交通 · 流线设计',senseId:'aerodynamic.s1',en:'The engineers tested a more aerodynamic shell in the wind tunnel, and the smoother shape reduced drag enough to extend the electric car’s range.',zh:'工程师在风洞中测试了更具流线型的外壳，较平滑的形状降低了阻力，足以延长电动车的续航。',structure:'The engineers tested a more aerodynamic shell in the wind tunnel / and the smoother shape reduced drag / enough to extend the car’s range.',grammar:'aerodynamic 修饰 shell 或 shape，表示空气流经时阻力较小；more 与形容词比较级搭配。',rationale:'外形降低空气阻力，符合 aerodynamic.s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aerodynamic shell reduce drag at high speed.','The aerodynamic shell reduces drag at high speed.','单数主语 shell 在一般现在时需搭配 reduces。')],quiz:[q('aerodynamic',1,1,'An aerodynamic car body is shaped to?','let air pass with less drag','stop all air from moving','make the car heavier','aerodynamic.s1 指减小空气阻力的形状。'),q('aerodynamic',2,1,'Why did engineers test the shell in a wind tunnel?','to study how air flows around it','to measure its soil aeration','to give it admittance','风洞能测试空气流动和阻力。'),q('aerodynamic',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','an aerodynamic wing','an aerodynamically wing','an aerodynamics wing','aerodynamic 是修饰 wing 的形容词。'),q('aerodynamic',4,1,'A streamlined helmet may be described as aerodynamic because it?','reduces resistance as air moves past','contains no air inside','is a study of naval command','该形容词可描述使空气较易流过的形状。')]});
D('aerodynamics',{etymology:{origin:'aerodynamics 由 aero-“空气”与 dynamics“动力学”构成，19世纪用于空气运动及物体在空气中运动的科学研究。',prefix:'aero-',root:'dynam-',suffix:'-ics',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aerodynamics'},contexts:[{domain:'物理 · 空气流动',senseId:'aerodynamics.s1',en:'The design team used aerodynamics to explain why the prototype lifted at the nose, then changed the wing angle before repeating the flight test.',zh:'设计团队用空气动力学解释原型机机头为何抬升，随后调整机翼角度，再次进行飞行测试。',structure:'The design team used aerodynamics to explain why the prototype lifted at the nose / then changed the wing angle / before repeating the test.',grammar:'aerodynamics 通常以复数形式出现，但学科名词常作单数用；study/use aerodynamics 是常见搭配。',rationale:'团队研究空气作用与飞机运动的关系，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','Aerodynamics explain how air moves around a wing, and it guides the design.','Aerodynamics explains how air moves around a wing, and it guides the design.','学科名称 aerodynamics 此处作单数整体概念，谓语用 explains。')],quiz:[q('aerodynamics',1,1,'Aerodynamics studies?','air motion and how objects move through air','the rules of marital conduct','the process of adding air to soil only','aerodynamics.s1 是研究空气及物体在空气中运动的学科。'),q('aerodynamics',2,1,'A race-car team consults aerodynamics to improve?','airflow and drag around the car','its admission policy','the taste of its fuel','空气动力学可以帮助理解汽车周围的气流与阻力。'),q('aerodynamics',3,1,'Which phrase is correct?','the aerodynamics of a wing','the aerodynamic of a wing','aerodynamicality of a wing','aerodynamics 是该科学领域的名词形式。'),q('aerodynamics',4,1,'Why test an aircraft design in a wind tunnel?','to measure aerodynamic forces and airflow','to determine whether bricks are dried','to appoint an admiral','风洞实验用于研究空气动力学表现。')]});
D('aerolite',{etymology:{origin:'aerolite 由希腊语 aer“空气”与 lithos“石头”组成，19世纪用于称呼从天空落下的石质陨石。',prefix:null,root:'aer- + lith-',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aerolite'},contexts:[{domain:'天文学 · 陨石',senseId:'aerolite.s1',en:'The museum’s aerolite came from a stony meteorite recovered after a bright fireball crossed the desert, and its cut surface revealed small mineral grains.',zh:'博物馆的这块石陨石来自一颗划过沙漠上空的明亮火流星，切面显露出细小的矿物颗粒。',structure:'The museum’s aerolite came from a stony meteorite recovered after a bright fireball crossed the desert / and its cut surface revealed mineral grains.',grammar:'aerolite 是可数名词，指石质陨石；描述其来源时可用 meteorite recovered after…',rationale:'对象是从天体落下的石质陨石，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aerolite were stored in a glass case beside the meteorite display.','The aerolite was stored in a glass case beside the meteorite display.','单数主语 the aerolite 应搭配 was。')],quiz:[q('aerolite',1,1,'An aerolite is a?','stony meteorite','kind of naval officer','mud brick dried in the sun','aerolite.s1 指石陨石。'),q('aerolite',2,1,'A museum labels a rock recovered after a meteorite fall as an aerolite. The rock came?','from a stony object that fell from space','from a city’s water-treatment tank','from a plant’s root system','aerolite 与从天而降的石质陨石有关。'),q('aerolite',3,1,'Which sentence uses aerolite correctly?','The aerolite was examined for mineral grains.','The aerolite administer the school.','The aerolite is an admiral’s title.','aerolite 是石质陨石的名词。'),q('aerolite',4,1,'A scientist studies an aerolite to learn about?','material from a stony meteorite','the history of advertising','how a meeting is postponed','该词指石陨石，可供天文学和地质研究。')]});
D('aeronautical',{etymology:{origin:'aeronautical 由 aeronautic 加形容词后缀 -al 构成；aeronautic 与 aero-“空气、飞行”及 Greek nautes“水手、航行者”相关。',prefix:'aero-',root:'naut-',suffix:'-ical',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aeronautical'},contexts:[{domain:'航空 · 工程',senseId:'aeronautical.s1',en:'The aeronautical engineer inspected the wing joints and control cables before the aircraft was cleared for its first test flight.',zh:'飞机获准进行首次试飞前，航空工程师检查了机翼接头和操纵钢索。',structure:'The aeronautical engineer inspected the wing joints and control cables / before the aircraft was cleared for its first test flight.',grammar:'aeronautical 修饰 engineer，表示与航空科学或飞机飞行相关。',rationale:'工程师的工作涉及飞机结构与飞行安全，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aeronautical engineer check every control cable before takeoff.','The aeronautical engineer checks every control cable before takeoff.','单数主语 engineer 在一般现在时需搭配 checks。')],quiz:[q('aeronautical',1,1,'Aeronautical engineering is connected with?','aircraft and the science of flight','advice about family matters','the construction of mud-brick houses','aeronautical.s1 指航空或飞行领域的。'),q('aeronautical',2,1,'An aeronautical chart would most likely be used by?','a pilot planning a flight','a cook preparing a meal','a court clerk scheduling a hearing','aeronautical 与航空和飞行有关。'),q('aeronautical',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','aeronautical research','aeronautically research','an aeronautic researchly','aeronautical 是形容词，可修饰 research。'),q('aeronautical',4,1,'An aeronautical engineer may inspect?','an aircraft’s control surfaces','a legal admission ticket','an advertiser’s campaign budget only','该形容词描述航空工程和飞行器相关工作。')]});
D('aeronautics',{etymology:{origin:'aeronautics 由 aeronautic 加名词后缀 -s 构成，名称结合 aero-“空气”与 Greek nautes“航行者”，指航空飞行的科学、技术或实践。',prefix:'aero-',root:'naut-',suffix:'-ics',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aeronautics'},contexts:[{domain:'科学 · 飞行',senseId:'aeronautics.s1',en:'Her aeronautics course combined flight theory with simulator hours, giving students practice in navigation, lift, and the effect of crosswinds.',zh:'她的航空学课程把飞行理论与模拟器训练结合起来，让学生练习导航、升力和侧风的影响。',structure:'Her aeronautics course combined flight theory with simulator hours / giving students practice in navigation, lift, and crosswinds.',grammar:'aeronautics 通常用复数词形表示航空学或飞行术这一学科。',rationale:'课程研究飞行理论与实际操作，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','Aeronautics are the science and practice of aircraft flight.','Aeronautics is the science and practice of aircraft flight.','表示学科的 aeronautics 虽以 -s 结尾，通常作单数名词。')],quiz:[q('aeronautics',1,1,'Aeronautics concerns?','the science and practice of flight by aircraft','the study of marital disputes','the process of adding air to soil only','aeronautics.s1 指航空学和飞行术。'),q('aeronautics',2,1,'A course in aeronautics might cover?','lift, navigation, and aircraft flight','how to assess an insurance claim','how to make an adage','航空课程会学习飞行原理与实践。'),q('aeronautics',3,1,'Which sentence treats aeronautics as a field of study?','Aeronautics is taught in the engineering school.','Aeronautics are a single aircraft.','Aeronautics is a person who sells tickets.','学科名 aeronautics 通常与单数 is 搭配。'),q('aeronautics',4,1,'A student studying aeronautics is learning about?','aircraft and flight','admittance rules for libraries','soil acidity','该学科研究航空器飞行的科学与实践。')]});
D('aeroplane',{etymology:{origin:'aeroplane 于19世纪末经法语 aéroplane 进入英语，构成包含 aero-“空气”与 plane“平面”；词名原先指空气中的平面或机翼，后指飞机。',prefix:'aero-',root:'plan-',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aeroplane'},contexts:[{domain:'交通 · 飞机',senseId:'aeroplane.s1',en:'The aeroplane climbed above the clouds after leaving the coastal airport, while passengers watched the shoreline disappear beneath the wing.',zh:'飞机离开海滨机场后爬升到云层上方，乘客看着海岸线逐渐消失在机翼下方。',structure:'The aeroplane climbed above the clouds after leaving the coastal airport / while passengers watched the shoreline disappear beneath the wing.',grammar:'aeroplane 是英式英语常用的飞机名词；美式英语常用 airplane。',rationale:'句中指有机翼和发动机、能够飞行的交通工具，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The aeroplane fly above the clouds on a clear morning.','The aeroplane flies above the clouds on a clear morning.','单数主语 the aeroplane 在一般现在时需用 flies。')],quiz:[q('aeroplane',1,1,'An aeroplane is a vehicle that?','flies using wings and an engine','moves only on railway tracks','is made from sun-dried mud','aeroplane.s1 指有翼、有发动机的飞机。'),q('aeroplane',2,1,'Which word is a common American variant of aeroplane?','airplane','admiral','aeration','airplane 是美式英语中常见的对应词。'),q('aeroplane',3,1,'Choose the correct sentence.','The aeroplane landed safely.','The aeroplane were landing safely.','The aeroplane is a type of proverb.','单数名词 aeroplane 与 landed 或单数谓语搭配。'),q('aeroplane',4,1,'Passengers board an aeroplane when they are about to?','travel by air','enter a soil pond','review an insurance claim','aeroplane 是用于空中旅行的飞机。')]});
D('aerospace',{etymology:{origin:'aerospace 是20世纪中期形成的复合词，由 aer(o)-“航空”与 space“空间”组合，涵盖飞机、航天器及其飞行空间和相关技术。',prefix:'aero-',root:'space',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aerospace'},contexts:[{domain:'产业 · 航空航天',senseId:'aerospace.s1',en:'The aerospace company hired materials scientists to test heat-resistant panels for both commercial aircraft and the next generation of launch vehicles.',zh:'这家航空航天公司聘请材料科学家测试耐热板材，供商用飞机和下一代运载火箭使用。',structure:'The aerospace company hired materials scientists / to test heat-resistant panels / for aircraft and launch vehicles.',grammar:'aerospace 作名词修饰 company，指航空与航天产业。',rationale:'公司业务涉及飞机和航天运载器，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'技术 · 飞行空间',senseId:'aerospace.s2',en:'Aerospace research must consider the thin upper atmosphere as well as the near-Earth region where satellites and high-altitude aircraft travel.',zh:'航空航天研究既要考虑稀薄的高层大气，也要考虑卫星和高空飞机运行的近地空间。',structure:'Aerospace research must consider the thin upper atmosphere / as well as the near-Earth region / where satellites and high-altitude aircraft travel.',grammar:'aerospace 也可指飞机运行的大气层及外层空间，或相关技术领域。',rationale:'研究范围包含飞机和卫星运行的空间，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-choice','The aerospace firm built only wooden furniture and had no connection to aircraft or spacecraft.','The furniture firm built only wooden furniture and had no connection to aircraft or spacecraft.','完全不涉及飞机、航天器或相关技术的公司不属于 aerospace industry。')],quiz:[q('aerospace',1,1,'An aerospace company may build?','aircraft and spacecraft','only kitchen furniture','admission tickets','aerospace.s1 指航空航天产业。'),q('aerospace',2,2,'Aerospace can refer to the region used by?','aircraft and spacecraft','only underground trains','people inside a library','aerospace.s2 涵盖飞机和航天器所处的空间及其技术。'),q('aerospace',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','aerospace engineering','aerospacely engineering','an aerospatiality engineering','aerospace 可修饰 engineering，形成常用复合搭配。'),q('aerospace',4,2,'A researcher in aerospace might study?','flight from the atmosphere into space','adultery law only','the right to enter a museum','该领域结合航空、航天器与飞行空间。')]});
D('aesthetical',{etymology:{origin:'aesthetical 是 aesthetic 加形容词后缀 -al 的形式；aesthetic 来自德语 ästhetisch/法语 esthétique，最终源于希腊语 aisthētikos“感知的”。',prefix:null,root:'aisthet-',suffix:'-ical',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aesthetical'},contexts:[{domain:'设计 · 审美标准',senseId:'aesthetical.s1',en:'The review considered the aesthetical value of the public sculpture, asking whether its materials and proportions suited the historic square around it.',zh:'评审考察了这座公共雕塑的审美价值，讨论其材料和比例是否适合周围的历史广场。',structure:'The review considered the aesthetical value of the public sculpture / asking whether its materials and proportions suited the historic square.',grammar:'aesthetical 修饰 value，表示与美感或审美评价有关。',rationale:'讨论关注雕塑的美学价值，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-formation','The committee discussed the aestheticaly value of the sculpture.','The committee discussed the aesthetical value of the sculpture.','aesthetical 是形容词；若需副词，拼写为 aesthetically，不能写 aestheticaly。')],quiz:[q('aesthetical',1,1,'An aesthetical judgment concerns?','beauty or artistic appreciation','the engine’s fuel pressure','a ship’s command rank','aesthetical.s1 表示与审美或美学有关。'),q('aesthetical',2,1,'Which question is aesthetical?','Does the sculpture’s shape look balanced?','Who has permission to enter the lab?','When will the court adjourn?','审美判断关注形式、比例与美感。'),q('aesthetical',3,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','aesthetical value','aestheticaly value','aesthetic valuefully','aesthetical 是可修饰 value 的形容词。'),q('aesthetical',4,1,'A design review focused on aesthetical qualities examines?','the work’s appearance and artistic effect','its insurance payment schedule','its oxygen release only','aesthetical 关联美感和艺术欣赏。')]});
D('aesthetically',{etymology:{origin:'aesthetically 由 aesthetic + -al 形成形容词，再加副词后缀 -ly；aesthetic 最终源自希腊语 aisthētikos“感知的”。',prefix:null,root:'aisthet-',suffix:'-ally',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aesthetically'},contexts:[{domain:'建筑 · 外观评价',senseId:'aesthetically.s1',en:'Aesthetically, the new station fits the old market square because its brick arches echo nearby buildings without copying their historic details.',zh:'从审美角度看，新车站与旧集市广场相协调，因为砖拱呼应了附近建筑，却没有照搬其历史细节。',structure:'Aesthetically / the new station fits the old market square / because its brick arches echo nearby buildings without copying their historic details.',grammar:'句首 aesthetically 表明评价标准是外观或美学；because 引出理由。',rationale:'评判的是车站与广场的视觉协调性，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'设计 · 美观呈现',senseId:'aesthetically.s2',en:'The cables were routed behind the panel so the control room would look aesthetically pleasing while remaining easy for technicians to maintain.',zh:'电缆被布置在面板后方，使控制室看起来美观，同时仍便于技术人员维护。',structure:'The cables were routed behind the panel / so the control room would look aesthetically pleasing / while remaining easy to maintain.',grammar:'aesthetically 修饰 pleasing，描述外观美观的方式。',rationale:'布线让控制室在视觉上更美观，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-formation','The new lobby is aestheticly pleasing to visitors.','The new lobby is aesthetically pleasing to visitors.','正确副词拼写为 aesthetically，不能漏掉词干中的 a。')],quiz:[q('aesthetically',1,1,'Aesthetically, a building is judged by?','its beauty and visual design','its permission to enter','its oxygen consumption alone','aesthetically.s1 表示从审美角度评价。'),q('aesthetically',2,2,'“The room is aesthetically pleasing” means it?','looks attractive','has been legally adopted','floats without a mooring','aesthetically.s2 表示外观美观地。'),q('aesthetically',3,1,'Choose the correct spelling.','aesthetically pleasing','aestheticly pleasing','aestheticaly pleasing','副词的标准拼写为 aesthetically。'),q('aesthetically',4,2,'A designer hides visible cables for an aesthetically clean room. The goal is?','to make the room look attractive','to raise the room’s oxygen level','to admit visitors without permission','这里 aesthetically 表示视觉上美观。')]});
D('aestivate',{etymology:{origin:'aestivate 于17世纪中期见载，来自拉丁语 aestivare“度过夏天”，源自 aestivus“夏季的”，与 aestus“热、暑气”相关。',prefix:null,root:'aestiv-',suffix:'-ate',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/aestivate'},contexts:[{domain:'动物 · 夏眠',senseId:'aestivate.s1',en:'During the hottest months, the desert snail aestivates beneath a layer of dry leaves, becoming active again when seasonal rain returns.',zh:'在最炎热的几个月里，沙漠蜗牛会躲在干叶层下夏眠，季节性降雨回来后才重新活动。',structure:'During the hottest months / the desert snail aestivates beneath a layer of dry leaves / becoming active again when seasonal rain returns.',grammar:'aestivate 是不及物动词，表示在炎热或干旱季节进入不活动状态；主语是单数 snail。',rationale:'蜗牛在高温季节休眠、雨季恢复活动，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The desert snail aestivate beneath dry leaves during the hottest months.','The desert snail aestivates beneath dry leaves during the hottest months.','单数主语 the desert snail 在一般现在时需用 aestivates。')],quiz:[q('aestivate',1,1,'An animal that aestivates during a hot dry season?','becomes inactive until conditions improve','flies to a colder country every night','is given permission to enter a building','aestivate.s1 指炎热或干旱季节的夏眠。'),q('aestivate',2,1,'A desert snail aestivates beneath leaves. It is?','resting in an inactive state during the heat','building a nest from aircraft parts','being trained for an aerobic class','夏眠能让动物避开炎热和干旱。'),q('aestivate',3,1,'Which sentence uses aestivate correctly?','Some snails aestivate through the dry season.','Some snails aestivation through the dry season.','Some snails are aestivates every morning.','aestivate 是表示夏眠的动词。'),q('aestivate',4,1,'When might a species aestivate?','during a hot or dry season','during a brief admiral’s speech','whenever it receives an advertisement','该词表示在炎热或干旱时段休眠。')]});
D('afar',{etymology:{origin:'afar 由 a- + far 构成，至少自古英语时期起用作“从远处、在远处”；a- 在此保留旧式副词构词形式。',prefix:'a-',root:'far',suffix:null,source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/afar'},contexts:[{domain:'观察 · 远处',senseId:'afar.s1',en:'From the ridge, we could see the lighthouse afar, its signal flashing beyond the fishing boats that were returning at dusk.',zh:'从山脊上，我们能看见远处的灯塔，它的信号灯在黄昏返航的渔船之外闪烁。',structure:'From the ridge / we could see the lighthouse afar / its signal flashing beyond the fishing boats returning at dusk.',grammar:'afar 作副词，表示在远处或从远处；可用于较文学的表达。',rationale:'灯塔位于观察者很远的地方，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-choice','The lighthouse stood afar from us, only a meter away across the path.','The lighthouse stood nearby, only a meter away across the path.','仅一米远属于 nearby，不是 afar（远处）。')],quiz:[q('afar',1,1,'A light visible afar can be seen?','from a long distance','only inside a closed box','after it has been adjourned','afar.s1 表示在远处或从远处。'),q('afar',2,1,'The sailors saw land afar. Land was?','far away','directly under the boat','inside the cabin','afar 描写远距离的位置。'),q('afar',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a voice heard afar','a voice afar to hear','an afar voicefully','afar 通常作副词修饰动作或状态。'),q('afar',4,1,'Choose the closest meaning of “from afar.”','from a great distance','from an adjoining room','from a legal advisor','afar 的核心是远处、远距离。')]});
D('affable',{etymology:{origin:'affable 于15世纪中期经古法语 affable 来自拉丁语 affabilis“容易交谈的”，源自 affari“对某人说话、交谈”。',prefix:null,root:'fari-',suffix:'-able',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/affable'},contexts:[{domain:'社交 · 待人亲切',senseId:'affable.s1',en:'The affable host greeted each late-arriving guest by name and made room at the crowded table without making anyone feel rushed.',zh:'这位和蔼的主人逐一叫出晚到客人的名字，并在拥挤的餐桌旁安排座位，没有让任何人感到匆忙。',structure:'The affable host greeted each late-arriving guest by name / and made room at the crowded table / without making anyone feel rushed.',grammar:'affable 修饰 host，表示待人友善、容易亲近。',rationale:'主人亲切接待来客，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'谈话 · 随和语气',senseId:'affable.s2',en:'Her affable conversation put the nervous applicant at ease, moving naturally from the interview questions to a discussion of the local community.',zh:'她亲切随和的谈话让紧张的求职者放松下来，自然地从面试问题聊到了当地社区。',structure:'Her affable conversation put the nervous applicant at ease / moving naturally from interview questions / to the local community.',grammar:'affable 也可修饰 conversation，表示谈话亲切、轻松。',rationale:'交谈气氛友好放松，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','The affable host welcome every visitor with a warm smile.','The affable host welcomes every visitor with a warm smile.','单数主语 the host 在一般现在时需用 welcomes。')],quiz:[q('affable',1,1,'An affable host is?','friendly and kind to guests','difficult to approach and hostile','a device for adjusting a lens','affable.s1 描写待人友好、和蔼可亲。'),q('affable',2,2,'An affable conversation is?','pleasant and relaxed','a formal naval command','a silent legal record','affable.s2 可形容轻松亲切的谈话。'),q('affable',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','an affable manner','an affably manner','an affability manner','affable 是形容词，可修饰 manner。'),q('affable',4,2,'Which person is most likely to be called affable?','a welcoming neighbor who chats comfortably','a guard who refuses to speak to anyone','a pilot studying aerodynamics','友善且容易交谈的人符合 affable。')]});
D('affecting',{etymology:{origin:'affecting 是 affect 的现在分词形容词；“感人、触动情感”义来自 affect“对感情产生作用”，该动词经法语或拉丁语 afficere 相关词形进入英语。',prefix:null,root:'fect/fac-',suffix:'-ing',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/affecting'},contexts:[{domain:'叙事 · 感人',senseId:'affecting.s1',en:'The documentary ended with an affecting scene in which the retired nurse returned to the village school where she had taught for forty years.',zh:'纪录片以一幕动人的场景收尾：退休护士回到她曾任教四十年的乡村学校。',structure:'The documentary ended with an affecting scene / in which the retired nurse returned to the village school / where she had taught for forty years.',grammar:'affecting 修饰 scene，表示能唤起怜悯、温柔或悲伤等感情。',rationale:'重返故地的场景打动观众，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('grammar','They described the documentary as an affecting.','They described the documentary as affecting.','affecting 在此作形容词补语，前面不应加不定冠词 an。')],quiz:[q('affecting',1,1,'An affecting story is likely to?','make readers feel tenderness or sadness','teach the laws of aerodynamics','give visitors permission to enter','affecting.s1 指能触动情感的。'),q('affecting',2,1,'Which moment is most likely to be affecting?','a long-separated parent and child meeting again','a routine list of office supplies','a neutral weather measurement','重逢容易唤起温柔或悲伤，具有感染力。'),q('affecting',3,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','an affecting farewell','an affectingly farewell','an affectional farewell only','affecting 可作形容词修饰 farewell。'),q('affecting',4,1,'A scene is affecting when it?','produces strong feelings in the audience','has no emotional effect','is made of stone from space','affecting.s1 强调引起情感反应。')]});
D('affectional',{etymology:{origin:'affectional 由 affection 加形容词后缀 -al 构成，表示与感情或情感联系有关；affection 经法语来自拉丁语 affectio，源自 afficere“影响、作用于”。',prefix:null,root:'fect/fac-',suffix:'-al',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/affectional'},contexts:[{domain:'心理 · 情感联系',senseId:'affectional.s1',en:'The study measured affectional bonds between foster parents and children separately from the practical duties involved in daily care.',zh:'研究把寄养父母与儿童之间的情感纽带，与日常照护中的实际职责分开测量。',structure:'The study measured affectional bonds between foster parents and children / separately from the practical duties / involved in daily care.',grammar:'affectional 修饰 bonds，强调感情联系而非职责或理性判断。',rationale:'研究对象是人与人之间的情感纽带，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-choice','The affectional bond was measured only by the number of bolts in the machine.','The mechanical connection was measured by the number of bolts in the machine.','机器螺栓数量衡量的是机械连接，不是 affectional（情感方面的）纽带。')],quiz:[q('affectional',1,1,'An affectional bond is primarily about?','emotional attachment','airflow around a wing','permission to enter a building','affectional.s1 指情感方面的联系。'),q('affectional',2,1,'A report separates affectional care from legal duties. Affectional care concerns?','feelings and emotional connection','the machine’s aerodynamic shape','the amount of oxygen in water','affectional 强调感情而非职责。'),q('affectional',3,1,'Choose the natural collocation.','affectional relationship','affectionalize relationship','affectionally relation','affectional 是形容词，可修饰 relationship。'),q('affectional',4,1,'Which situation is affectional?','a child’s emotional bond with a caregiver','a plug connecting two sockets','a ruling against a contractor','此词描述感情方面的关系或因素。')]});
D('affective',{etymology:{origin:'affective 由 affect 加形容词后缀 -ive 构成，指与情感有关或能引发情感；affect 经拉丁语 afficere 相关词形进入英语。',prefix:null,root:'fect/fac-',suffix:'-ive',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/affective'},contexts:[{domain:'心理 · 情绪反应',senseId:'affective.s1',en:'The therapist asked clients to record affective responses to the photographs separately from the thoughts they had about each image.',zh:'治疗师请来访者把自己对照片的情绪反应，与他们对每幅图的想法分别记录。',structure:'The therapist asked clients to record affective responses to the photographs / separately from the thoughts / they had about each image.',grammar:'affective 修饰 responses，表示与感情而非纯思考有关。',rationale:'记录的是情绪反应，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'艺术 · 情感感染',senseId:'affective.s2',en:'The film’s affective power came from its quiet final scene, which made the audience grieve for characters it had come to know slowly.',zh:'这部电影的情感感染力来自安静的结尾场景，它让观众为逐渐熟悉的人物感到悲伤。',structure:'The film’s affective power came from its quiet final scene / which made the audience grieve / for characters it had come to know slowly.',grammar:'affective 也可表示能引起强烈情绪反应的。',rationale:'影片场景促使观众产生悲伤，符合 s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('word-formation','The survey recorded an affect response to each image.','The survey recorded an affective response to each image.','作形容词修饰 response 时需用 affective，而非名词 affect。')],quiz:[q('affective',1,1,'An affective response is connected with?','feelings rather than thought alone','air pressure around an aircraft','the right to enter a room','affective.s1 指情感方面的。'),q('affective',2,2,'An affective scene in a film may?','cause strong feelings in viewers','measure the film’s length','turn the film into an acronym','affective.s2 可形容引起情感共鸣的。'),q('affective',3,1,'Choose the correct adjective.','affective response','affect response','affection responseful','affective 是修饰 response 的形容词。'),q('affective',4,2,'Which phrase most clearly uses the emotional-impact sense?','the affective force of the ending','the aerodynamic shape of the ending','the admittance of the ending','affective 可表示作品带来的情感力量。')]});
D('affinity',{etymology:{origin:'affinity 经古法语 affinité 来自拉丁语 affinitas，原指姻亲关系或相邻关系；其基础 affinis 表示“相邻、相连”，由 ad- 与 finis“边界”构成。',prefix:'ad-',root:'fin-',suffix:'-ity',source:'Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/affinity'},contexts:[{domain:'兴趣 · 自然喜爱',senseId:'affinity.s1',en:'She felt an affinity for languages from childhood, often learning a new greeting from travelers and remembering the stories behind unfamiliar expressions.',zh:'她从小就对语言有天然的喜爱，常向旅行者学一句新问候，并记住陌生表达背后的故事。',structure:'She felt an affinity for languages from childhood / often learning a greeting from travelers / and remembering stories behind unfamiliar expressions.',grammar:'affinity for + 人、群体或活动表示天然喜爱或亲近感。',rationale:'人物自然而然喜欢语言，符合 s1。',sourceType:'authored'},{domain:'化学 · 亲和性',senseId:'affinity.s2',en:'The compound has a strong affinity for water, so it dissolves readily and forms a stable solution at room temperature.',zh:'这种化合物对水有很强的亲和性，因此容易溶解，并在室温下形成稳定溶液。',structure:'The compound has a strong affinity for water / so it dissolves readily / and forms a stable solution at room temperature.',grammar:'affinity for 在科学语境中也表示结构相似或物质结合倾向。',rationale:'物质容易与水结合，符合 affinity.s2。',sourceType:'authored'}],mistakes:[m('collocation','She has an affinity of classical music and studies it every evening.','She has an affinity for classical music and studies it every evening.','表示对某活动或对象的自然喜爱时，常用 affinity for。')],quiz:[q('affinity',1,1,'A person with an affinity for music?','naturally likes or feels close to it','is legally required to perform it','has no ability to hear it','affinity.s1 指天然的喜爱或亲近感。'),q('affinity',2,2,'A chemical has an affinity for water when it?','tends to combine with or dissolve in water','avoids all contact with water','is appointed to command a ship','affinity.s2 可指物质间结合的倾向。'),q('affinity',3,1,'Which preposition completes the common phrase? “an affinity ___ languages”','for','at by','from of','常见搭配为 affinity for。'),q('affinity',4,2,'Two materials share an affinity in structure. They have?','a similarity or tendency to associate','no properties in common','a shared advertising budget','affinity.s2 可指结构相似或相互亲和。')]});
